<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">29 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 29 January, from 757 to 1916.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/757">757 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,269 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The rebel An Lushan is killed in a plot by his son</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/an-lushan">An Lushan</a>, the Tang general who had rebelled in 755 and proclaimed himself emperor of Yan, was killed in a plot involving his own son, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/an-qingxu">An Qingxu</a>. The rebellion he began continued under his successors until 763.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/an-lushan">An Lushan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/an-lushan-rebellion">An Lushan Rebellion</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">904 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,122 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sergius III seizes the papacy from the antipope Christopher</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the behest of Theophylact I of Tusculum, Sergius III seized the papal throne from Christopher, who had himself deposed Leo V. His reign fell in a time of violence and disorder in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">Papacy</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/946">946 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,080 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Abbasid caliph al-Mustakfi is deposed and imprisoned</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> al-Mustakfi, who had reportedly intrigued against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muizz-al-dawla">Mu'izz al-Dawla</a> with some of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buyid-dynasty">Buyids</a>' Daylamite officers, was deposed on Mu'izz al-Dawla's orders. He spent the rest of his life as a prisoner in the caliphal palace.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/tsar" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tsar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1676">1676 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">350 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Feodor III becomes Tsar of Russia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexis-of-russia">Tsar Alexei</a>, his sickly 14-year-old son Feodor succeeded him. In a short reign he abolished the system of ranking nobles by ancestry, paving the way for his half-brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1820">1820 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">206 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George III dies at Windsor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Blind and suffering from mental illness, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-iii">George III</a> died after a reign of almost 60 years, which had seen the loss of America and victory over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>. His son the Prince Regent became George IV.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1845">1845 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">181 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edgar Allan Poe's 'The Raven' is published</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Poe's poem of a grieving lover and a talking bird appeared in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> Evening Mirror. It made him famous almost overnight, though it earned him little money.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1886">1886 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">140 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Karl Benz files a patent for his motor car</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Benz applied for a German patent on a 'vehicle powered by a gas engine', his three-wheeled Motorwagen. It is generally regarded as the first practical petrol-driven automobile.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1900">1900 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">126 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The American League of baseball is organised</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Ban Johnson reorganised a minor league as the American League, with eight teams. It declared itself a major league in 1901 and met the National League in the first World Series in 1903.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1916">1916 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">110 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Zeppelin raid kills civilians in Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A German airship bombed eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, killing more than twenty people in the Ménilmontant area. It was the last Zeppelin raid on the city, which strengthened its air defences.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 29 January <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-henry-prince-of-orange"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-henry-prince-of-orange.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Frederick Henry, Prince of Orange</span><span class="tp">1584–1647</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/amalie-elisabeth-of-hanau-munzenberg"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/amalie-elisabeth-of-hanau-munzenberg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Amalie Elisabeth of Hanau-Münzenberg</span><span class="tp">1602–1651</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/william-mckinley"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-mckinley.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">William McKinley</span><span class="tp">1843–1901</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 29 January <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/george-iii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/george-iii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">George III</span><span class="tp">1738–1820</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/leopold-ii-grand-duke-of-tuscany"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/leopold-ii-grand-duke-of-tuscany.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Leopold II, Grand Duke of Tuscany</span><span class="tp">1797–1870</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/evelyn-baring-1st-earl-of-cromer"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/evelyn-baring-1st-earl-of-cromer.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Evelyn Baring, 1st Earl of Cromer</span><span class="tp">1841–1917</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ioannis-metaxas"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ioannis-metaxas.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ioannis Metaxas</span><span class="tp">1871–1941</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/prince-aimone-duke-of-aosta"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/prince-aimone-duke-of-aosta.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Prince Aimone, Duke of Aosta</span><span class="tp">1900–1948</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
